<title>BELGIUM: EU clears KNP buy of German, Italian paper firms.</title>
<headline>EU clears KNP buy of German, Italian paper firms.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Monday it had approved plans by Dutch paper and packaging company NV Koninklijke KNP BT to acquire two graphic paper distribution subsidiares from the U.K.'s Bunzl Group -- Wilhelm Seiler GmbH of Germany and Bunzl Italia SpA.  </p>
<p>&quot;The Commission found that KNP BT's increasing market position both in Italy and Germany is not likely to result in a dominant position on those markets, since other distributors as well as paper producers will ensure sufficient compeition,&quot; the Commission said in a statement.</p>
<p>Among KNP's competitors are IGEPA, Schneider Soehne, Paper Union and Classen in Germany and AWA and Burgo in Italy.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom 32 2 287 6800</p>
</text>
